    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_db8989f3",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts the destruction of the World Trade Center towers during the 9/11 attacks, overlaid with text that reads, 'i know you shouldn't laugh at 9/11 jokes but their just, plane hilarious.' This juxtaposition uses the horrific visual of a national tragedy to deliver a joke that trivializes the event. The intent is to create humor by playing on the word 'plane' (as in airplane) and 'plane hilarious,' which is a pun that mocks the gravity of the event. This is harmful because it minimizes the suffering and loss of life associated with 9/11, potentially causing emotional distress to survivors, victims' families, and the broader public. The meme's intent is to provoke laughter at the expense of a deeply traumatic historical event, which can be seen as a form of disrespect and insensitivity. The overall intent is to elicit humor through dark, insensitive wordplay, which is harmful due to its potential to trivialize a catastrophic event and its victims.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_0e8ddcd3"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
